-- title:
--   Cusp place on the ∞-component is unramified over X₀(M')
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$ and a positive integer $M'$ not divisible by $q$, and a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $K \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ be the intermediate field obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field $\mathbb{Q}$-adjoin-$\mathrm{intFormRatiosC}$ of $\Gamma_0(q^2M')$, and let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ whose maximal ideal contains $q$ and is generated by $\varpi$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $\mathrm{jq} = q^{-1}\cdot \mathrm{jNumQ}$, assumed nonzero. Let $W_0$ be the valuation subring of $K$ consisting of those $f$ for which there are power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal and $f \cdot y = x$ as Laurent series over $L$ (the Gauss ring of $A$-integral $q$-expansions). Let $K_0 \subseteq K$ be the analogous field for $\Gamma_0(M')$, with inclusion given by $hle_0$. Let $w$ be a place of $K$ over $L$, i.e. a proper valuation subring of $K$ containing $L$ that is a principal ideal ring, with $\mathrm{ord}$ the associated normalised integer valuation; assume $\mathrm{ord}_w(j^{-1}) > 0$. Finally let $y$ be a maximal ideal of the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$, containing the image of $\varpi$, containing every element of that subalgebra lying in the nonunits of $W_0$, and containing every element $b$ of it with $\mathrm{ord}_w(b) > 0$. Then the ramification index of $w$ along the inclusion $K_0 \hookrightarrow K$ — the least $n > 0$ for which some nonzero $f \in K_0$ has $\mathrm{ord}_w(f) = n$ — equals $1$.
--
--   This is the unramifiedness of a cusp of $X_0(q^2M')$ over $X_0(M')$, for a cusp place specialising into the closed point $y$ of the pole chart on the $\infty$-type component of the reduction: the incidence and width arithmetic of cusps with $q^2 \mid c$ forces ramification index one. It is the $\Gamma_0$-level form of the corresponding statement for the fields $X_H$, and feeds the full-level version [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.ramificationIndexAlong_inclusion_eq_one_of_ord_jInvChartInf_pos_of_forall_ord_pos_mem_of_forall_mem_nonunits_gauss_xH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.ramificationIndexAlong_inclusion_eq_one_of_ord_jInvChartInf_pos_of_forall_ord_pos_mem_of_forall_mem_nonunits_gauss_xH).
